WEBVTT

00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:16,020
I remember my genetic report, the BR, the BRCA was highlighted, but the genetic test that my

00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:27,060
oncologist ran because I was under 50 showed BRCA as negative, were the test looking at different

00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:33,220
genes. So remember, the BRCA genes, there's dozens and dozens of BRCA genes, they're gene

00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:38,820
family. So when we say, oh, I am defects in my rocket genes, that means you have defects in

00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:44,180
that BRCA gene family. Now, they're only looking like I said before, typically, they're only

00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:48,740
looking at a couple of those genes, even when they run the test, they're only testing for a couple

00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:54,100
of those genes in that gene family. To me, that's silly. Oh, just because these are the most

00:00:54,100 --> 00:01:00,340
researched and these ones are, you know, the most research to me, the issues and those are negative.

00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:04,820
Well, if you had tons of defects in some of the other ones, then it's like, okay, well,

00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:10,420
this could be an issue. So again, when you have defects in a gene, it doesn't mean the gene's not

00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:15,460
going to work, but doesn't mean that, you know, you're doomed for a life. It just means that you have

00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:20,340
a greater chance of that gene not functioning as well as if you didn't have any defects in it.

00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:28,340
You don't know why the medical profession truncates things so often. It makes no sense to me.

00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:33,780
Is it really, they're already charging you a bloody fortune to run a test like that? They're

00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:39,300
charging your insurance bloody fortune. Why don't they do it? Well, it's just like having somebody go

00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:45,620
into the ER and they do, uh, I've seen this so many times, they did this. They went into the ER with

00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:50,100
all these issues. They do a CBC, but they don't do a differential. What the heck? It costs you like

00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:56,980
another $2 to do it. I just don't understand it. They go to the, they pick the cheapest thing.

